 "_comment": "Group 5 question-flow golden routes. Each route starts on rb_document_inventory with topography C69.2 and gives the macro steps a clerk takes there; expect is what the case must end on: kind, code, behaviour, referral group, outstanding tests, basis of diagnosis and the evidence credited. A macro is one screen answered: tickset = boxes ticked on a checklist (ctxRow 1 picks the inadequate-specimen row), opt = one list answer, imaging = features and diversion boxes ticked then Continue. Recorded on main f19df62 for the first version (41 routes, branch flow-g05), then rewritten on 14 October 2026 for the registrar's rulings of that day (RQ1 the two 'tissue has since been obtained' answers are gone, RQ2 and RQ6 the enucleation and retinocytoma screens are one tick screen, RQ3 the referral wording is a tick list with a named non-malignant cause first, RQ7 the first screen offers four boxes, RP1 and RP3 a required imaging feature that is not stated reads the referral note when the file holds one, RP2 pseudohypopyon needs tissue, RQ4 a mimic pattern beside a pattern that needs tissue reads as tissue, RP4 a liquid biopsy report has its own box and answer, RP6 the inadequate-specimen row beats a ticked histology report). Every expectation was written from the ruling and the Pathway, not copied from a run. A `ruling` field names the ruling a route came from; a route without one is unchanged in meaning from the recorded 41.",
